			"Message": "docs(Maintain): Convert module header comment to rustdoc in Run module\n\nReplace the verbose C-style block comment banner (80+ lines of architectural boilerplate with RESPONSIBILITIES, ARCHITECTURAL ROLE, IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS sections) in `Source/Run/mod.rs` with an idiomatic Rust doc comment (`//!`).\n\n- Collapse the declarative header into a concise module overview with a submodule purpose table linking to each of the 9 child modules (CLI, Constant, Definition, Environment, Error, Fn, Logger, Process, Profile).\n- Drop the stale architectural boilerplate (Dependencies, Dependents, Design Patterns, Thread Safety sections) that duplicated crate-level documentation.\n- Remove the stripped module-declarations comment that preceded the `pub mod` lines.\n\nThese changes improve code clarity without altering any runtime behaviour.",
